 We get the following: 
\begin{equation*}\int \frac{\cos x}{\sqrt{1-\sin x}}\, dx=\int(-2)\, du=-2\cdot \int 1\, du=-2u+c\end{equation*}  
 Therefore \begin{equation*}\int \frac{\cos x}{\sqrt{1-\sin x}}\, dx=-2\sqrt{1-\sin x}+c\end{equation*}  
