{"input_text": "Question: I would like to calculate the de De Rham cohomology groups of projective real space $\mathbb{RP}^{n}$. Well, i know all groups of De Rham cohomology os $n$-sphere $\mathbb{S}^{n}$ and that the map $\pi:\mathbb{S}^{n}\to \mathbb{RP}^{n}$ (the restriction to the projection map on $\mathbb{S}^{n}$) is a smooth submersion. With these tools, can I compute the cohomology groups of real projective space? How can I do this? 

