Answer: Because if a parabola, say $f(x)$, has absolute maximum at point $x_0$, then $-f(x)$ should have absolute minimum at $x_0$ and vice versa. But when we multiply $f(x)$ by $(-1)$, we don't flip the parabola over it's turning point. We are taking the symmetry of it with respect to the $x-$axis. 
